Keep the AAC priming when seeking an MP4/M4A track to its start.

A seek to the start of an AAC track landed on the first presented packet,
after the encoder priming (an edit list's discarded pre-roll, or the start
padding recorded only in iTunSMPB). The decoder then started without its
overlap frame and the first ~20-40 ms of the track faded in from silence.
mpv performs such a seek when it opens the first file of a playback session.
Step back to the first packet in that case, so the seek matches a read from
the beginning; the existing start-padding skip removes the priming again.

--- a/libavformat/mov.c
+++ b/libavformat/mov.c
@@ -11685,6 +11685,18 @@
             break;
 
         timestamp = next_ts;
+    }
+
+    /* Seeking to the start must include the encoder priming (an edit list's
+     * discarded pre-roll or the iTunSMPB start padding), exactly as when reading
+     * from the beginning; otherwise the first decoded frame lacks its overlap
+     * and fades in. The start padding skip then removes the priming again. */
+    if (st->codecpar->codec_type == AVMEDIA_TYPE_AUDIO) {
+        while (sample > 0 &&
+               ((sti->index_entries[sample - 1].flags & AVINDEX_DISCARD_FRAME) ||
+                av_rescale_q(sti->index_entries[sample].timestamp - sti->index_entries[0].timestamp,
+                             st->time_base, (AVRational){ 1, st->codecpar->sample_rate }) < sc->start_pad))
+            sample--;
     }
 
     mov_current_sample_set(sc, sample);
